course: dictionary
lesson: 7531
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives prawn two senses: a small sea animal, and an Australian slang phrase. Context tells you which one is meant. «After two hours of Roblox curled over his tablet like a prawn, Kai stood up» uses prawn to describe a bent, curled-up shape, so the comparison is the clue.
explain: Now look at «About half of the fish people eat now comes from fish farms, such as salmon, carp and prawn farms.» Here prawn is an animal raised for food. The words farms, eat and fish tell you it is about food, not a toy or a pet.
explain: When you meet a word with more than one meaning, ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Swap your choice in and read it again. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
fact: A prawn is a small sea animal with a thin shell, long feelers and ten legs.
fact: Prawns turn pink when they are cooked, and people eat them as food.
fact: In Australia, «Don't come the raw prawn» is slang meaning «don't try to fool me».
fact: Prawn can also be a verb, but it is rare: to prawn means to fish for prawns.
fact: Some people are allergic to prawns, so they must never eat them.
exercise: «After two hours of Roblox curled over his tablet like a prawn, Kai stood up.» What does prawn help us picture here? | A loud, sudden noise | A fast, racing car | A tall, straight tree | *A bent, curled-up shape
exercise: Dad says, «Don't come the raw prawn with me, I saw you eat the biscuits.» What does he mean? | Please cook me a prawn dinner | Stop talking about the sea | *Don't try to fool me | Go and fish for prawns
exercise: «About half of the fish people eat now comes from fish farms, such as salmon, carp and prawn farms.» What is a prawn farm? | A place where prawns are sold as toys | A shop that sells fishing rods | A farm that grows only potatoes | *A place where prawns are raised for food
test: What is a prawn? | A small land animal with fur and four legs | A type of sandwich bread | *A small sea animal with a thin shell, long feelers and ten legs | A sea plant with bright green leaves
test: What colour does a prawn turn when it is cooked? | Green | Black | Blue | *Pink
exam: Which sentence uses prawn to mean an animal people eat? | Kai sat curled like a prawn all afternoon | *Fish farms raise salmon, carp and prawns for people to eat | Don't come the raw prawn, mate | Prawn is a rare verb meaning to fish
